course: dictionary
lesson: 11651
title: Artisan: skilled makers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An artisan is a skilled worker who makes things by hand. Read the words around it to find the clue. «The artisan carved a wooden bowl by hand.» The words carved and by hand tell you the artisan works with skill, not with a machine.
explain: Artisan can also be a describing word. «My aunt buys artisan bread from the little bakery on our street.» Here artisan tells you how the bread was made: by hand, in small amounts, in a traditional way.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Does «made by a skilled worker by hand» fit? If yes, you have the right meaning. If it does not, check the clues again or look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: An artisan is a skilled worker who makes things by hand.
fact: Examples of artisans are carpenters, potters and weavers.
fact: In medieval towns, artisans joined guilds: groups such as blacksmiths, shoemakers and masons.
fact: «Artisan» can also be an adjective, as in «artisan bread» or «artisan cheese».
fact: Shops write «artisan» on food to show that it was made by hand, often in small amounts.
exercise: «The artisan carved a wooden bowl by hand.» What is an artisan? | A tool used for cutting wood | A machine in a factory | A shop that sells bowls | *A skilled worker who makes things by hand
exercise: Mum says, «This cheese is artisan.» What does artisan mean here? | Very old and dusty | Made by a robot in a huge factory | Bought cheap from a supermarket | *Made by hand in small amounts, in a traditional way
exercise: Which worker was an artisan in a medieval town? | A cartoon character on television | A cashier counting money in a bank | A pilot flying an aeroplane | *A blacksmith in a guild
test: «The weaver was an artisan who spent months on each rug.» What does artisan tell us about the weaver? | *She was a skilled worker who made the rug by hand | She was a famous film star | She was a very fast machine operator | She worked in a shop selling rugs
test: In «artisan bread», what kind of word is artisan? | A word for a place | *A describing word, an adjective | A name for a person | A doing word, a verb
exam: «The shoemaker, a skilled artisan, sewed each boot by hand.» Which clue shows that artisan means skilled and handmade? | The shoemaker was in a shop | Boots are worn on feet | *Sewed each boot by hand | The boots were a gift
